{ SH4 (GOG PC) - Stackable Items (entry 7360)                                                    [v3]
  Game: SILENT HILL 4.exe (32-bit, base 400000, no relocations). Static RE only - see notes.txt here and
  ..\..\research\inventory\inventory_re.txt. Works with or without Extend Toolbelt (7310, pockets_v6.cea), in either
  enable order: the two scripts never patch the same bytes and never scan each other's patched bytes.

  What it does
   * Same items stack. An item that enters the toolbelt joins the first entry with the same ID that holds
     less than st_max (99); what does not fit becomes a new entry as usual. With Extend Toolbelt on,
     Toolbelt 2 is searched too, so a stack stays on one page.
   * A chest take-out moves the chest stack (up to st_max) as ONE toolbelt entry; the rest stays in the
     chest. The game moved one "unit" per take-out (1, or a gun's capacity), so a Revolver x93 came out as
     one revolver per take-out (6 rounds each) while the chest kept the rest.
   * Using an item takes ONE off its entry in the game already (candle, Sword, healing, keys, a shot, the
     item thief). New here: a stacked golf club / Wine Bottle that breaks, or a used-up Saint Medallion,
     also costs only one - the next one is fresh, the in-use mark stays - and the broken club / bottle is
     added as its own item when there is room.
   * Counts above 1 are drawn on the toolbelt and in the chest for every item.
   * v2: a floor pickup with a full toolbelt still works when the whole pickup fits into a stack of the same
     ID (st_pickfull); otherwise the game's "too many items" stays. Saint Medallions also stack in the chest
     (the game merged chest medallions only up to 1): one chest entry, the lower condition is kept.

  Switches (1 = on): st_merge, st_takeout, st_break, st_show, st_pickfull (v2).   st_max = 99 (stack size;
  keep it 12..999).
  Counters: st_mgn merges, st_tkn take-outs, st_bkn stacked items that broke, st_lost broken items dropped
  (no room), st_pfn full-belt pickups let through (v2). st_force = 1: [DISABLE] runs even while a stack of more than 10 stealable items is on the
  toolbelt (the game's item thief has room for 10 x 10 - see notes.txt).

  HOOKS (address - what - why)
   516D20  give item        pickups and script gifts join a stack first
   4F6D70  chest take-out   the stack as one entry (up to st_max), joining a stack first
   4F62E0  take-out check   OK when the item can join a stack, even with a full belt; bar slot it flies to
   511F7E  take-out anim    call: how many leave the chest (does the chest row close?)
   511947  take-out anim    call: how many the chest row shows as left
   4F6A30  break            stacked weapon / medallion: count - 1, next one fresh, broken one added
   4F5DB2  use one          an entry left with count > 0 never keeps condition 0 (the game removes such an
                            entry one per frame)
   463607  item thief       call: count per entry capped at 10 (the game's list has 100 places)
   514D62  belt rebuild     mark "show the count" when count > 1
   51410F  count drawing    draw the count of any item when count > 1
   4D1110  floor pickup     call (v2): "belt full?" answers "no" when the whole pickup joins a stack
   4F6579  chest merge      (v2) medallions merge like ammo (up to 999); the merged stack keeps the lower
                            condition
   5133CB  chest put-in UI  (v2) a medallion that will join a chest stack: no new chest row is animated
  v3: on enable, stacks already on the belt get their count shown at once (before, the numbers only came
      back after the belt changed, e.g. a chest move).
}
[ENABLE]
aobscanmodule(st_givep,SILENT HILL 4.exe,53 57 8B 7C 24 0C 57 E8 ?? ?? ?? ?? 57 8B D8 E8 ?? ?? ?? ?? 83 C4 08 85 C0 0F 85 E2 00 00 00 57 E8)
aobscanmodule(st_takep,SILENT HILL 4.exe,57 8B 7C 24 08 0F B6 04 FD B6 7B 3D 01 85 C0 74 0E 50 E8)
aobscanmodule(st_chkp,SILENT HILL 4.exe,8B 44 24 04 85 C0 75 04 83 C8 FF C3 89 44 24 04 E9)
aobscanmodule(st_predp,SILENT HILL 4.exe,8B 46 10 8B 08 51 E8 ?? ?? ?? ?? 2B D8 83 C4 08 85 DB 7E 07)
aobscanmodule(st_leftp,SILENT HILL 4.exe,8B 55 00 52 8B F0 E8 ?? ?? ?? ?? 2B F0 83 C4 08 85 F6 0F 8E)
aobscanmodule(st_brkp,SILENT HILL 4.exe,83 FE FF 74 60 0F B6 14 F5 66 7B 3D 01 33 C0 85 D2 74 21)
aobscanmodule(st_usep,SILENT HILL 4.exe,49 66 85 C9 66 89 0C C5 64 7B 3D 01 77 32 0F B6 CA)
aobscanmodule(st_thiefp,SILENT HILL 4.exe,3B FD 74 24 56 E8 ?? ?? ?? ?? 8B D0 83 C4 04 85 D2 75 07)
aobscanmodule(st_barp,SILENT HILL 4.exe,85 F6 74 4B FF 05 80 EC 08 01 8A 03 0C 01)
aobscanmodule(st_drawp,SILENT HILL 4.exe,8B 89 80 00 00 00 49 83 F9 10 77 53 0F B6 89 7C 41 51 00)
aobscanmodule(st_pickp,SILENT HILL 4.exe,E8 ?? ?? ?? ?? 85 C0 74 5F 8B 44 24 04 56 57 8B B8 20 04 00 00 50 E8)
